[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says it is one bug with one fix queued. Read report by report, it
holds more than one problem, and each needs its own fix. The queued parser fix closes only `parser`.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known. The queued fix covers <code>parser</code> only. Each problem below has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first, so a day-first date comes out with day and month swapped: through the app, by email
and through the booking-v2 form. The queued fix is for this one.

**`hint` — booking-v3 prints a month-first hint under its date field.** Only tenants on
booking-v3, and only reports through that form. People type what the hint tells them, month
first; the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The result looks the same as
`parser`, so subject-line merging put it in #4471, but the parser fix does not touch it. The fix
is the hint (or reading the field the way it hints).

**`shift` — the date lands a day early.** Day and month are not swapped: the weekday moves back
by one, a client in another time zone gets a different day for the same meeting, an invite
arrives before the booking was made. That is a date stored or sent as a midnight time and
converted across time zones. Neither code path in `causes.ts` produces it, so the cause table on
#4471 files these under the tenant's cause with a footnote. The table above counts them the
desk's way: where they are filed, and again as `shift`.

## Why the merge hid them

- Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) cannot see
  any of this: every problem arrives as "wrong day".
- Intake tags come from the reporter's browser, not the tenant. The table counts by tenant and
  form; compare its two columns.
- The cause table on #4471 picks the biggest group as the ticket's cause and marks the rest
  "no ticket of its own". They have tickets now.

## What to do

- Keep #4471 for `parser`; the other problems have their own tickets above.
- Ship the parser fix, and check booking-v3 and the time-zone path separately: the parser fix
  does not reach them.

